{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1288913-you-know-what-solars-need-another-craft-charm","id":1288913,"title":"You know what Solars need? Another Craft charm!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-17T06:52:08-08:00","id":1288913,"title":"You know what Solars need? Another Craft charm!","content":"Inspired while re-reading a bit about how Tolkien elves didn't see their crafts as distinctly magic, but rather inhuman extensions of skill.<br /> <br /> <b>Perfection of Artifice</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m; <b>Mins:</b> Craft 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> The Art of Permanence<br /> <br /> Men marvel at the magics wrought by the Exalted, but to the true craftsman there is no clear line between artifacts and more mundane items- only the skill needed to realize more subtle and intricate designs.<br /> <br /> A Solar may use Perfection of Artifice to undertake a Project to create or repair an Artifact, replacing the need to have dots in Craft (Artifacts).<br /> <br /> A repurchase at Essence 5 allows a character to replace the need for Craft (First Age Artifice) and Terrestrial Circle Sorcery as well when undertaking construction or repair of such marvels. This does not replace the need for any sorcerous workings that are necessary, and may require the Lawgiver to work in cooperation with a sorcerer in order to make such projects possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T10:42:02-08:00","id":1288949,"title":"","content":"I like the inspiration, but I don't quite get the motivation. Why a Charm, when the existing mechanics are already there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T12:45:17-08:00","id":1288979,"title":"","content":"My biggest issue is that this is... spend XP to not spend XP on something else? Why would I want to buy this over just using Supreme Celestial Focus to buy Crafts (Artifact) with gxp so I can spend my normal XP on something that actually does something?<br /> <br /> Why would I use a Charm repurchase to wave the requirement for TCS... instead of just buying TCS considering how much just getting that one Charm does for you?<br /> <br /> If all this Charm is going to do, is to let you spend XP to skip requirements that you can meet by.... spending XP... it's kinda pointless, and it doesn't really capture the inspiration either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T15:19:05-08:00","id":1289012,"title":"","content":"If I may offer an alternate suggestion, perhaps a charm that allows a Solar to work minor supernatural blessings into their mundane craft without them needing to be artifacts? Something like what the Art of Enchantment or the ritual of elemental empowerment did in 2E. (Because most of them aren't worth a working).<br /> <br /> So solar made armor might be only a quarter the weight yet just as strong, or a solar made blade might be self-sharpening and never rust. The crafter could probably, technically, explain how they didn't do magic, they burned ever-living wood from the far East when hardening it or what not and it is entirely &quot;mundane&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T17:43:29-08:00","id":1289044,"title":"","content":"The Art of Permanence (the pre-req listed) and it's own pre-reqs already do a lot of investing minor magic into mundane objects, even if mostly in terms of making them resistant to damage, use, and so on. You can already make a blade that's always sharp, or a torch that will burn for the ages, and similar minor things with the existing Charms.<br /> <br /> There isn't a lot of room between what's available from those Charms, and being low level Artifacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T18:30:49-08:00","id":1289050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1288913-you-know-what-solars-need-another-craft-charm?p=1289044#post1289044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Art of Permanence (the pre-req listed) and it's own pre-reqs already do a lot of investing minor magic into mundane objects, even if mostly in terms of making them resistant to damage, use, and so on. You can already make a blade that's always sharp, or a torch that will burn for the ages, and similar minor things with the existing Charms.<br /> <br /> There isn't a lot of room between what's available from those Charms, and being low level Artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's exactly why I chose the Art of Permanence as the pre-req. That felt like the boundary between 'minor magic stuff' and 'capital-A Artifacts'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T18:36:12-08:00","id":1289052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1288913-you-know-what-solars-need-another-craft-charm?p=1288979#post1288979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest issue is that this is... spend XP to not spend XP on something else? Why would I want to buy this over just using Supreme Celestial Focus to buy Crafts (Artifact) with gxp so I can spend my normal XP on something that actually does something?<br /> <br /> Why would I use a Charm repurchase to wave the requirement for TCS... instead of just buying TCS considering how much just getting that one Charm does for you?<br /> <br /> If all this Charm is going to do, is to let you spend XP to skip requirements that you can meet by.... spending XP... it's kinda pointless, and it doesn't really capture the inspiration either.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is 100% to save xp. Not even gonna front on that.<br /> <br /> As to why you'd buy it instead of Supreme Celestial Focus; two fold. One, SCF is down a different tree, and Craft is so large that you can only really effectively go down one of the main branches. Two, because there's a feeling-difference between having Craft (Artifact) vs Craft (Weaponsmith) - one is a kind of conceptual understanding of What Are Artifacts, and the other is just being so adept at making swords that you start making capital-S Swords.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T21:08:43-08:00","id":1289084,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d dump the repurchase, the entire point of First Age Artifice this edition is that it does in fact have a different \u201cfeel\u201d from \u201cnormal\u201d artifacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T22:48:51-08:00","id":1289104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1288913-you-know-what-solars-need-another-craft-charm?p=1289050#post1289050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's exactly why I chose the Art of Permanence as the pre-req. That felt like the boundary between 'minor magic stuff' and 'capital-A Artifacts'</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a bad choice, but I'm not sure it's the best choice for the original mechanics you presented (at least not alone). Expanding on the tree leading up to Art of Permanence with more similar bonuses you can put on items so they live between mundane equipment and Artifacts could be cool. Buying a Charm to ignore prerequisites for crafting actual Artifacts doesn't really fit by itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1288913-you-know-what-solars-need-another-craft-charm?p=1289052#post1289052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is 100% to save xp. Not even gonna front on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that it doesn't really save you XP. It makes it look like you're going to save XP by not having to buy up two extra Crafts. But skipping SCF means skipping five Crafts worth of savings, and skipping TCS (which you have to qualify to buy anyway) means skipping on a huge amount of front loaded power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As to why you'd buy it instead of Supreme Celestial Focus; two fold. One, SCF is down a different tree, and Craft is so large that you can only really effectively go down one of the main branches. </div> </div> </div>I don't agree. Crafters in 3e aren't going to go down deep in multiple trees, but there's a few Charms that are too good to pass up. Sublime Transference (which means you'll qualify for SCF even if you could skip it), Supreme Perfection of Craft (which means getting CNNT and SCF), and Bright-Forging Prana are all way too good to skip even if their trees aren't your focus. Supernal Crafts can get you all of those for nine of your starting Charms.<br /> <br /> Sublime Transference + SPoC ensure you always have the cxp you need for what you're doing, and you have CNNT for being able to craft on the fly. Bright-Forging Prana means you have access to the basic low level dice-trick in its pre-req, and can either grab a bunch of other dice-tricks, or whatever other Charms you want from the overly large choices around and aren't reliant on throwing the Excellency at every roll.<br /> <br /> So skipping SCF for your custom Charm because you're not going to get SCF's pre-req is more of a trap because it means you're skipping Sublime Transference and SPoC which is a really bad idea... and SCF is a huge XP saver on its own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Two, because there's a feeling-difference between having Craft (Artifact) vs Craft (Weaponsmith) - one is a kind of conceptual understanding of What Are Artifacts, and the other is just being so adept at making swords that you start making capital-S Swords. </div> </div> </div>And to make artifact swords in the game you need both. Crafting an Artifact without a relevant mundane craft is not a good idea.<br /> <br /> Someone that saw your Charm and thinks it means they can make low level Artifacts without going outside the Repair/Rebuild tree is... going to be sorely mistaken in how effective their character is going to be. They aren't going to be making much in the way of &quot;Sword!&quot; when you take the rest of the crafting system into account.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, a character with the Charm spread above can actually... be so adept at making swords that they learn the secrets of magical swords <i>from making swords</i> and then have a much easier time actually making those Artifact swords in the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T04:35:37-08:00","id":1289144,"title":"","content":"Hrm.<br /> <br /> Alright, fair enough. I'm convinced; this was probably a poor design direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T07:33:30-08:00","id":1289183,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I'm agreed that this is a brilliant prompt; here's a slightly different Charm that hopefully does the prompt justice.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Numinous Smith Meditation</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: - (12m 2wxp); Mins: Craft 5, Essence 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Permanent</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Permanent</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms: The Art of Permanence</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The hands of the Lawgiver breath life and majesty into that which she makes, to call any of her works mundane is an insult to her peerless artistry. A comb carved out of shell becomes both a beautiful ornament, and able to rearrange hair with ease; statues stand out as almost-living embodiments of their subject, exulting them in the eyes of their subjects; even armour seems to turn away cuts and scrapes as its engravings and embellishments strike fear into the heart of their enemy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Charm upgrades its prerequisite, granting it the following effects if used with the increased cost of twelve motes, two white experience points:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unmatched Tool:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Any item created by this Charm is exceptional; merely meeting the difficulty is enough for the finished work to count as an Exceptional Item, both for bonuses from use, and for Crafting rewards.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sublime Art:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The item lasts forever, not just as a symbol of the Lawgiver, but of her motivations for crafting it. The Craft roll for making it acts as an instil roll against those viewing the item for the first time, creating or strengthening a Tie towards the item\u2019s user, or another target if the storyteller permits, in keeping with the emotional context: armour strikes fear in its enemies, or respect for the protected wearer, jewellery might arouse fascination, whilst a sturdy outfit force those viewing it to view the wearer as rugged and dependable. This effect of multiple items with similar contexts does not enforce multiple instil attempts, as the effect of otherworldly perfection affects the onlooker less with repetition. This instil roll cannot be enhanced with non-Craft Charms.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Peerless Armoury: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Weapons and Armour crafted by this Charm gain some improvement over mundane items; weapons deal an additional die of withering damage on a successful attack, and armour grants its wearer one Hardness.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Thoughts:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At Essence 4, this Charm breaks some of the game\u2019s rules, namely making armour and weapons that are better than mundane. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It felt like a natural improvement on the Art of Permanence to be, as that Charm already creates what are effectively magic items, but this one instil them with a little more power.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Sublime Art effect is really strong: it effectively forces most opponents to resist this effect with willpower, as Craft rolls have too many successes to count.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">An alternative effect that I was thinking of for Peerless Armoury was to create the advantage of a speciality when acting in accordance with a Principle that the Solar and the user share, but I felt that that effect would be too complicated.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Armour created by this Charm would render its wearer immune to the flux of the Dragon-Blooded, making it a very powerful investment.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019m tempted to add an effect, or a second Charm, that grants the creation an Evocation or a frankly supernatural ability</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12692,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12692-whybover","user":"Whybover","date":". 02-18-2019, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12692-whybover","name":"Whybover","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T13:59:21-08:00","id":1289301,"title":"","content":"I might be worth breaking each upgrade, and let the player pick which ones to apply. If I'm making, say, awesome lock-picks, Unmatched Tool isn't worth 12m, 2wxp for something I might be able to do without Charms, and can definitely do with much less investment. Peerless Armory isn't going to apply. And I wouldn't really want to pay for Sublime Art on tools meant for sneaky activities.<br /> <br /> I would probably rephrase Sublime Art slightly to require a bit more action before the effect kicks in. This would help the ST adjudicate the type of Tie from the context. Rather than 'view the item for the first time,' I would have it be, 'view the item being used for the first time.' Seeing a beautiful broach in a drawer doesn't really help you figure out how to handle the instill action. Seeing that broach as the single adornment on a somber outfit at a funeral service provides a lot more guidance on where to go with it.<br /> <br /> I would also be very careful with Peerless Armory and it mucking with the base numbers. Hardness 1 is also barely functional as a bonus. Perhaps in keeping with Unmatched Tool, rather than breaking the rules here, allow the crafter to add a Tag to the item it wouldn't normally have. Additional Tags on weapons and armor can give you an edge without messing with the base numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T03:40:53-08:00","id":1289457,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your thoughts!<br /> <br /> <b>Sublime Art</b>, you're totally right. How about we go further to enforcing context, hijacking another mechanic that makes it clearer:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sublime Art: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The item lasts forever, not just as a symbol of the Lawgiver, but of her motivations for crafting it. <i>With an appropriate stunt</i>, the Craft roll for making it acts as an instil roll against those viewing the item, creating or strengthening a Tie towards the item\u2019s user, or another target if the storyteller permits, in keeping with the emotional context: armour strikes fear in its enemies, or respect for the protected wearer, jewellery might arouse fascination, whilst a sturdy outfit force those viewing it to view the wearer as rugged and dependable. Multiple items with similar contexts do not reapply multiple instil attempts, as the effect of otherworldly perfection affects the onlooker less with repetition. This instil roll cannot be enhanced with non-Craft Charms.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Unmatched Tool</b> is a side-benefit for dumping 6m1wxp over the original Charm, allowing you to not drop the Excellency on this roll. It's underwhelming in terms of bonuses, I agree.<br /> <br /> Awesome Lock-Picks are an interesting one. They definitely force a weird question. I hope the Sublime Art change above helps them be more awesome, but fundamentally if you're making lockpicks, you're probably wanting to jump to artefact ones, or jump down to Art of Permanence (6m1wxp to make them unbreakable).<br /> <br /> I'm not sure mixing and matching is all too advantageous, and <b>Peerless Armoury</b> is never applied to things that aren't weapons/armour, but I see your point about messing with the base numbers. My thought process for giving Hardness 1 was that it made a cool way of giving the &quot;minimum entry fee&quot; that some effects, such as anima flux, require to avoid, without actually making the armour all that better.<br /> I'd initially thought of granting an extra tag, but I decided against it because: tags that are good to add are often a little complicated, or the balanced tag; tags might get combined in ways that made less sense, but you're right that it's not really a great fudge; I'd definitely consider rewriting the Charm to allow adding a tag to weapons. For Armour, however, the tags are a little dull. Concealable, Silent, and Buoyant; I'd probably take a point of Hardness to render myself immune to the threat of things like flux instead unless I was a sailor, a thief, or planning on not wearing my Sublime Art armour for show.<br /> <br /> If you were to mix and match, the only benefit would be making Peerless Armoury weapons/armour that don't get Sublime Art, I'm not sure it's worth calling out that that's okay, especially with the <b>Sublime Art</b> change above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12692-whybover","name":"Whybover","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}